	(text "U1 Raspberry Pi Pico (H) · RP2040 · 40 pinos · 2 x 20"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 115.3 181.366 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
				(color 30 40 48 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "06492613-e101-4f28-8c89-46c9765f5113")
	)
	(text "02 · RASPBERRY PI PICO · MÓDULO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 52.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 6 6)
				(thickness 1.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0a837d72-1351-4169-990e-9fb0bc1b7eb3")
	)
	(text "    boost -> 3V3 (PWR_FLAG on GND, VSYS and VBUS for the ERC)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 197.866 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 60 68 74 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0da6a160-6aba-425f-b55b-7a12719dac24")
	)
	(text "1. U1 Raspberry Pi Pico / Pico H (RP2040, 40 pins) plugged into the shield on female headers. Power comes from the Pico: USB -> VBUS -> VSYS, on-board buck-"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 195.072 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 60 68 74 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "16e0c21d-bc8f-4bb2-ae0b-d42d0de4ea41")
	)
	(text "3. GP26 / GP27 / GP28 are also ADC0 / ADC1 / ADC2 (reference ADC_VREF). RUN low = reset; 3V3_EN low = 3V3 regulator off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 206.248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 60 68 74 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1874bf51-9a92-4b70-9de0-a1132605e307")
	)
	(text "4. IMPORTANT: terminals are wired straight to the RP2040 pins: 3.3 V logic, not 5 V tolerant, no protection."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 209.042 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 60 68 74 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3a929ee8-dcf2-4bc4-8cb1-0cc1faee837e")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 192.024 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
				(color 30 40 48 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3d967a88-8e6d-401d-bf22-8577fe3c1b82")
	)
	(text "2. Every Pico pin goes to a screw terminal (sheet 03). Nets use the Pico pin names (GP0 ... GP28, RUN, 3V3_EN, ADC_VREF, VSYS, VBUS). AGND is tied to GND as"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.586 200.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 60 68 74 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6bc8a088-6cc1-4086-b9c8-2821de74e29e")
	)
	(text "GND · VSYS · VBUS (vêm do Pico / USB)"
